="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="f9449537-232c-43f0-88cc-83696b315387" class="r-1jnu9po alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h5>Balance Your Hormones*</h5></span></div><div data-rid="a9a45f4a-c2e5-4860-898e-a6f3b259cbbe" class="r-1g3pe8a"><div data-rid="eaf09bab-3d01-4a59-87ee-68ed13231097" class="r-13jt9y0" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="17ed5b14-34ac-498e-84a0-18cde3ded4da" aria-controls="replo-:R1vdolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-q3u52d"><div data-rid="11624c9c-cc7a-4579-bd9f-a2a53e5c4269" class="r-1s8gllx alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What happens?</p></span></div><div data-rid="3d8c07d1-da9f-4a3a-9056-a664acf352e1" class="r-1o9hn57"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-wksef2" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1vdolr2:"><div data-rid="fa5c043b-2220-4ef9-bb93-cf439e5571cd" class="r-n1py57"><div data-rid="dc06327f-f970-4d62-bc3b-ea6f28bb78e6" class="r-x4ln2f alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Your hormones naturally rise and fall each month. But when oestrogen rises too high (often under everyday stress, hectic schedules, bad sleep, or poor diet), it triggers an overproduction of prostaglandins — the main driver behind deeper cramps and inflammation.<br><br>The result? With this natural balance lost, you´re left facing heightened cramping, and fewer defenses against pain flares. f you don’t have a condition like PCOS or endometriosis, studies indicate that the difference between someone with debilitating cramps and someone who barely notices theirs comes down to prostaglandin levels.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="5b74cca3-3005-4d46-882e-07b04e097efc" class="r-1eml18x" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="c2c18395-878d-4e97-ad12-f74586c28768" aria-controls="replo-:R2vdolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-yk1zk5"><div data-rid="75ab68bb-5e0e-4b76-b0b6-6a30499b4f1d" class="r-ql1ylu alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How monthlies helps</p></span></div><div data-rid="466218cf-667e-4b45-b8fd-d64a90abc81f" class="r-fgsb9g"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-e25eur" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R2vdolr2:"><div data-rid="64280b6a-4c16-4718-bf6d-ab26a606cd91" class="r-1oh4417"><div data-rid="5696ef37-d30c-48db-adc7-81c3b7b64323" class="r-nc7m0u alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Formulated with scientifically backed ingredients like <strong>Lemon Balm, Broccoli Seed Extract, B-Complex, Myo-Inositol, Choline, and Flaxseed</strong>, monthlies supports hormonal balance at its core—optimising oestrogen metabolism, promoting healthy progesterone, and supporting stress management.*<br><br>As your hormonal pathways are optimised, you're less prone to overactive cramping and inflammation from the start, unlike TENS which only blocks pain signals after cramps begin, setting the stage for cramps you barely even notice.*</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="9208eee4-bec9-4c29-8961-548eba849fcc" class="r-ta2d8t" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="e60ec4e3-b729-478a-b701-ccb9c332cafc" aria-controls="replo-:R3vdolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1bhuza4"><div data-rid="f9c3f20a-ae95-4a26-b626-d1fc0f795896" class="r-1mfbca0 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Clinical study highlight</p></span></div><div data-rid="72b2f3bd-bbe9-44f6-8687-347902d1bea6" class="r-jxotqb"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-121yvlc" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3vdolr2:"><div data-rid="38287b1e-4e92-426e-b83b-96a354cfd2ee" class="r-6s9mcu"><div data-rid="84f7d0a7-023a-49c1-a51d-76e05067b930" class="r-1udc65m alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Lemon Balm (found in monthlies): A double-blind randomized, placebo-controlled trial was performed on 100 high school girls and found that after 3 months, Lemon balm decreased PMS intensity scores by 67.3%. In another double-blinded placebo-controlled trial, 87% of participants in the treated group reported improved sleep quality, compared to 30% in the placebo group.*</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="inactive" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="radix-:Rolr2:-trigger-50b60960-e28a-476d-b5c6-07373ba8a9e91" id="radix-:Rolr2:-content-50b60960-e28a-476d-b5c6-07373ba8a9e91" tabindex="0" style="display:none"><div data-rid="4c0863e3-9027-4899-a9d1-9100cef7ae9d" class="r-xbh8z8"><div data-rid="71d9ff93-f80f-4303-860d-dda363375bb6" class="r-1cdu9tq"><div data-rid="57a0a762-ac1a-4e3e-8176-632ba5099f97" class="r-1ptjjq9"><div data-rid="7cfadf47-637f-4fc0-b275-4dd11f51a641" class="r-q6fslx"><picture data-rid="88d53d53-2d27-4fb5-8edf-b7556c395183" class="r-1om04e"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0708/7462/8371/files/v3_1_a36178d0-95b9-4783-ac76-8038a7e2e39f.webp?v=1739282201&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0615/3951/6642/files/Frame_9914145.webp?v=1720629119&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0615/3951/6642/files/Frame_9914145.webp?v=1720629119&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0615/3951/6642/files/Frame_9914145.webp?v=1720629119" alt="Supplement bottle in a garden, highlighting ginger, turmeric, and aniseed extracts." class="r-1vru0p5" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="0875a954-27a6-497d-a391-1e3044048843" class="r-aab2ep alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h5>Tame Prostaglandins*</h5></span></div><div data-rid="5a4bd57c-9352-4416-bf81-4524217a9949" class="r-2ybn5v"><div data-rid="6e1e621d-5412-4ed8-91b5-09c659f336f3" class="r-akc23c" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="7fd01b4b-c585-4804-8c74-ea4d2f22d3e6" aria-controls="replo-:R1vlolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-ie0ujj"><div data-rid="52c4af62-ba97-4ecf-adca-674b55371792" class="r-1xn6rrc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What happens?</p></span></div><div data-rid="545f96ab-06a0-4887-aaa2-7d1d107cf767" class="r-7bsw82"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-jjyz3i" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1vlolr2:"><div data-rid="b4bf9898-4a7e-4713-9591-43a1d1dde69e" class="r-iesira"><div data-rid="9ae1994c-7cfa-4e02-951e-542fd3fdacd4" class="r-azonlz alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Prostaglandins are essential and help your uterus shed its lining. However, when they surge — due to an an overactive COX-2 enzyme — they directly intensify cramps, sharpen pain signals, and make them more frequent.</p><br><p>Painkillers work by blocking prostaglandins after they’ve spiked, often hitting COX-1 (needed for stomach protection) along with COX-2. This can lead to side effects like indigestion or ulcers —while leaving hormonal and nutrient imbalances unresolved, so the cycle of pain keeps repeating.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="7ee49347-419a-405f-b420-c11e60ab75a0" class="r-z19c15" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="57858a32-d63a-4c22-b4e1-0f1ebb33e0f3" aria-controls="replo-:R2vlolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-63jn4j"><div data-rid="69ce5c29-9d72-47fb-a21c-7d6cc2df3f63" class="r-6aqiis alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How monthlies helps</p></span></div><div data-rid="6ec6d972-6a1e-4f1b-a1a3-949408f35a97" class="r-1xe4fke"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-5e4ytn" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R2vlolr2:"><div data-rid="d4f2194e-da64-4ae0-904a-f0ba050be96e" class="r-1gkikhn"><div data-rid="eeecdda8-fae0-429b-9cbf-d55a2c5e8e64" class="r-24o49f alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Formulated with <strong>potent anti-inflammatory</strong> support from Ginger Root Extract, Turmeric, and Aniseed, monthlies helps combat inflammation— with Ginger and Turmeric <strong>selectively favoring COX-2 inhibition to safeguard your stomach lining.*</strong><br><br>And because monthlies is designed for daily use — unlike painkillers — it works to keep COX-2 in check all month long, <strong>helping manage discomfort during your period while also addressing pain before it even begins.*<br></strong><br>By calming pain amplifiers at their source, monthlies supports less intense contractions, lower inflammation, and helps ease the nerve sensitivity that magnifies cramps — without the side effects you can get from painkillers. And unlike TENS machines that require you to stop activities to apply electrodes, <strong>monthlies works continuously from within.*</strong></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="e18e24a1-9214-4d54-ac34-a8d1155f994f" class="r-8witva" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="a9d0160e-580f-471e-b4f4-ea74d641692b" aria-controls="replo-:R3vlolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1wggx7p"><div data-rid="eac06372-7b3f-4db9-957c-63991c2ff6eb" class="r-1ffpez4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Clinical study highlight</p></span></div><div data-rid="17819b61-7bad-4426-a578-c8dc64969e94" class="r-gitig5"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-8iqztk" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3vlolr2:"><div data-rid="87eae4e8-574b-4b95-9ab7-84a344144641" class="r-1q1xhhi"><div data-rid="c2df4bbe-fa8f-4448-9e8e-9ca3d3dbe6cf" class="r-l762o6 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Ginger (found in Monthlies): A systematic review of 11 studies found there was no significant difference between ginger and NSAIDs (non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs) in decreasing pain intensity during menstruation. Additionally, studies showed that ginger reduced menstrual bleeding volume to the same degree as Mefenamic acid, a common pain medication. This suggests ginger offers comparable relief to pharmaceutical options without their side effects.*</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="inactive" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="radix-:Rolr2:-trigger-6f944ca4-86f0-46dd-a8a0-92db50d10f192" id="radix-:Rolr2:-content-6f944ca4-86f0-46dd-a8a0-92db50d10f192" tabindex="0" style="display:none"><div data-rid="821cf5a3-6954-4b05-abb4-a49694380be7" class="r-1q9o737"><div data-rid="f0d86488-7c41-4ada-bda9-53e6a0d8b3dc" class="r-1nk0imn"><div data-rid="203017ef-39fa-436f-bd64-d29335c0dd7a" class="r-15zfrn8"><div data-rid="0c4d0ae8-51ff-4af0-9481-2294150bc164" class="r-1p8bqif"><picture data-rid="65f10aaa-2e56-404d-8a94-4aa1f12c0fe1" class="r-drorr4"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0708/7462/8371/files/trustpilot.webp?v=1739021094&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0615/3951/6642/files/Frame_9914145.webp?v=1720629119&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0615/3951/6642/files/Frame_9914145.webp?v=1720629119&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0615/3951/6642/files/Frame_9914145.webp?v=1720629119" alt="A hand holding a drink with a positive review about Monthlies supplements." class="r-xgoy8f" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="05937fd1-43a8-4f71-8f67-7a71b09fcbc7" class="r-3kr4ci alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h5>Fill Micronutrient Gaps*</h5></span></div><div data-rid="66358ad1-e1c8-49e9-89dd-247419d96b06" class="r-zig2dt"><div data-rid="c170408e-4d01-4286-b3e4-9645d243a584" class="r-hhbhw1" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="920da74d-f4e7-4ec6-9c7b-4b6182ac1dcb" aria-controls="replo-:R1vtolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-fds4mr"><div data-rid="8fb23b64-cda8-4b66-9b38-7fa120c6b7ce" class="r-xufs2p alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What happens?</p></span></div><div data-rid="63094f5d-747f-43b1-be3a-2497f6c2c61d" class="r-b1d2dz"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-14wv35t" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1vtolr2:"><div data-rid="cc54a849-f468-4cb2-acb1-9514126d5918" class="r-sljdha"><div data-rid="2e025b0f-d7f8-4efa-977b-e7a62ca74192" class="r-119g4yp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>A woman's body relies on micronutrients to manage cramps, energize muscles, and regulate inflammation. But monthly blood loss, combined with fast-paced living or less-than-ideal nutrition, can leave reserves depleted. <strong>A 2024 study led by Harvard researchers found that many UK women have at least five major micronutrient gaps.*</strong></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="dd85e4e2-57df-4fce-bf13-4c857977c812" class="r-1sqj87j" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="78dca47f-c8cb-4a69-99f8-61226edbd1d6" aria-controls="replo-:R2vtolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1ibdp42"><div data-rid="61829f1e-1b58-4c89-b8e0-2075227d87b5" class="r-1qvqqn7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How monthlies helps</p></span></div><div data-rid="4ddfd48f-bad4-4571-8284-6e9bfc96a146" class="r-bp5z61"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-twxz74" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R2vtolr2:"><div data-rid="518747f8-72d6-4d96-aa6c-5d44a1e048f4" class="r-15nrws7"><div data-rid="83b7d84c-1fa1-4836-9233-f58cc9f57a4b" class="r-1gza8hw alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Packed with 26 scientifically backed ingredients, monthlies is the UK's most comprehensive formula for women’s health —all in a once-daily drink.<br><br>By<strong> </strong>replenishing<strong> </strong>essential micronutrients like<strong> Magnesium, Zinc, Iron, the entire Vitamin B Complex, and Vitamins D3 + K2, </strong>monthlies helps strengthen muscle function, energy production, and hormonal balance.*<br><br>This results in better control over cramps, calmer inflammation, hormonal regulation, clearer skin, fewer mood swings, and overall more optimal, more comfortable cycles — addressing multiple aspects of your cycle simultaneously, unlike TENS which can only target cramping pain in one area at a time.*</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="8fb3ced7-bb7e-4350-b6d5-b22d7741ef07" class="r-1qglq99" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="440f165c-6880-493e-b189-324ed3578f2d" aria-controls="replo-:R3vtolr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1yzdo2m"><div data-rid="bb1e2298-5818-4688-b0c1-d6425c827430" class="r-1pme1gr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Clinical study highlight</p></span></div><div data-rid="01f1e343-3a11-4230-913b-10272e03cbd0" class="r-7r9eup"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-fiup26" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3vtolr2:"><div data-rid="9dfa64ee-ae50-4a37-988a-84c1a5690344" class="r-1z0a6yq"><div data-rid="16cedec6-5a8f-45d5-8b88-f163991af030" class="r-1y485nt alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Calcium (found in monthlies): A systematic review of 14 studies (8 interventional, 6 observational) found that women with PMS have lower serum calcium levels and that calcium supplementation significantly reduces both the incidence and severity of PMS symptoms, underscoring a protective role for calcium in PMS management. In a randomised crossover trial of calcium carbonate, 73% of women had fewer symptoms after 3 months. Calcium eased low mood, bloating, and pain before menstruation, and also reduced menstrual cramps.*</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="1ff2f37a-4d50-4679-bc9f-f1b258bbba07" class="r-10i547r"><button data-rid="2f6f8f0a-31ce-4a53-a331-08a8394f4b41" tabindex="0" role="link" class="text r-jhnmm6 alchemy-rte"><div data-rid="e531b064-824f-4aa6-96d5-9635cbba0526" class="r-1uyt7cg"><div data-rid="6644e7de-6d52-4daf-9b97-009d127a5b80" class="r-jexfzj"><div data-rid="5ae32f87-16d9-4f21-950a-0c7247381a47" class="r-alsga3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Claim Offer</p></span></div></div></div></button><div data-rid="13c99b34-5824-4a8d-b2f4-a9c14b2b755d" class="r-1cwkdqd"><div data-rid="e66939aa-78a7-41f5-80d6-b12c51e9ae1e" tabindex="0" role="link" class="r-9syns1 alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontsize:12px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontweight:700;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-lineheight:16px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2